# 🔥 Kerberoasting – Service Account Analysis

## 📌 Overview
Kerberoasting targets service accounts with Service Principal Names (SPNs).

---

## 🎯 Objective
Identify weak service account configurations.

---

## 🧭 Workflow (High-Level)

1. Identify accounts with SPNs
2. Request service tickets (authorized lab)
3. Extract ticket data
4. Analyze password strength

---

## 🔍 What to Look For

### 🔑 Target Accounts
- Service accounts
- Accounts with SPNs
- Legacy systems

---

### ⚠️ Weakness Indicators
- Weak password policies
- No password rotation
- High privilege service accounts

---

## 📊 Evidence Indicators

- Kerberos ticket requests
- Unusual authentication patterns
- Large volume of ticket activity

---

## 🛡️ Detection

- Monitor Kerberos logs
- Detect abnormal ticket requests
- Alert on service account abuse

---

## 🔐 Prevention

- Strong passwords (20+ chars)
- Managed service accounts
- Regular rotation

---

## 🧠 DPCI Notes

- Correlate logs with user activity
- Document accounts targeted
- Include MITRE mapping in report
